node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.log

# Collected Showdown replays. Deliberately never committed: no licence covers
# the replay logs themselves (MIT applies to Showdown's server code, not to
# battle data), so this repository must not redistribute them. Re-collect with
# `data/collect.py`; the manifest records exactly what was fetched and when.
data/replays/

# Cached dex dumps, one per regulation's mod, regenerated on demand.
data/dex*.json

# Teams harvested from the replay corpus. Derived from unlicensed battle logs,
# so they inherit the same constraint the logs carry: local research use, never
# redistributed. Rebuild with `champions_ai.data.harvest` from a local corpus.
data/harvested_teams.txt

# Frozen evaluation pools. Same constraint as the teams they are built from:
# derived from unlicensed battle logs, so local research use only, never
# redistributed. Rebuild with `harvested_pool(..., cache=...)`.
data/pool-*.txt

# Team files worked on locally -- a candidate for a tournament, or one lifted
# out of a harvested pool to scout. The second kind inherits the corpus's
# constraint (unlicensed logs, never redistributed), and the first is the
# user's own competitive work, which is not this repository's to publish.
data/*team*.txt

# Ability priors derived from the corpus. Aggregate statistics rather than
# logs -- `data/collect.py` notes those are a different question -- but kept
# out of the repository anyway, because it is a *measurement of a corpus that
# is not published* and should be rebuilt from whatever corpus is to hand
# rather than inherited. `data.priors.build_ability_priors` over
# `harvest.gather_evidence` regenerates it.
data/priors-*.json

# Field priors -- which species predicts which weather or terrain -- for the
# same reason and on the same terms. `data.priors.build_field_priors` over the
# replays regenerates it; `experiments/0048-team-preview-field/build.py` is the
# script that does.
data/field-priors-*.json

# Mega Evolution rates per species, on the same terms: a measurement of an
# unpublished corpus, rebuilt rather than inherited.
# `experiments/0052-team-preview-megas/build.py` regenerates it.
data/mega-priors-*.json

# Usage statistics downloaded from Smogon (items, natures, Stat Point spreads).
# Third-party data, used for local research the way the replays are and never
# republished; `experiments/0057-pool-from-usage/fetch.py` downloads it again.
data/usage/

# Tournament open team sheets (RK9 public team lists). Third-party data like the
# replay corpus: read locally to scout against a real event's field, never
# committed or republished.
data/tournaments/
